Subject: [PATCH 0/2] arm64: errata: Fix two wrong Kconfig names

Two entries in the arm64 silicon-errata table
(Documentation/arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst) name Kconfig symbols that
no Kconfig file defines.  I checked every Kconfig name in the table:
these are the only two.

The GIC-700 #2941627 entry names ARM64_ERRATUM_2941627; that workaround
is a GIC driver quirk, selected at runtime from the GIC's IIDR, so
there is no symbol to name.  The Falkor E1041 entry names
QCOM_FALKOR_ERRATUM_1041 and drops the "E" from
QCOM_FALKOR_ERRATUM_E1041.

Patch 1 sets the GIC-700 Kconfig column to "N/A", as the table already
does for workarounds that have no Kconfig symbol; patch 2 fixes the
Falkor spelling.  Both are documentation changes with no behaviour
change, and the column widths are unchanged.  The hardware for these
workarounds is not available here, so this is based on the tree and the
commit history, and no build was run.

Both hunks are the same kind of fix in the same table, so squash them
into one patch if you would rather have it that way.

The changes and the changelog text were produced with an AI coding
assistant (Hermes Agent, model deepseek-v4.1-flash) working from the
tree and the git history.  I reviewed the diff and the reasoning, and I
am responsible for the submission.


